# Networking Task

Task: Configure DNS search domains for the secondary network interface.

- Using netplan, configure the DNS search domains `{{search_domain_1}}` and `{{search_domain_2}}` on the interface `{{interface}}`.
- Create a new netplan configuration file; do not modify the existing files in `/etc/netplan`.
- The search domains must be active on that link (visible to systemd-resolved) and must persist across reboots.
- Do not modify the primary network interface or the default route.
